# ===[ Ensemble Stacking ]=====================================================
* 'Ensemble stacking' is a technique used to combine multiple models to
  generate predictions.
  - It's a common technique of ensemble learning, as "bagging" and "boosting".

                      +-------------------+
                      | Ensemble Learning |
                      +---------|---------+
                                |
          +---------------------+---------------------+
          |                     |                     |
     +-----------+         +----------+          +----------+
     |  Bagging  |         | Boosting |          | Stacking |
     +-----------+         +----------+          +----------+
     - Random Forest       - AdaBoost            - MLP
                           - Gradient Boosting   - Meta-Model
                           - XGBoost

  # INFO:[ Stacking ]----------------------------------------------------------
  # - This technique is called stacking because the models are literally      |
  #   arranged in 'layers (stacks)'.                                          |
  # ->> where the output of one layer becomes the input of the next layer     | 
  #                                                                           |
  #   |> [ Layer 1: (level 0)]: X -> model_1, model_2 ... |-> predictions     |
  #   |> [ Layer 2: level(1) ]:                                               |
  #                             [ predictions ]                               |
  #                                   |                                       |
  #       [ instead of of averging them we stack them into another model ]    |
  #                                   |                                       |
  #                             [ meta-model ]                                |
  #                                   |                                       |
  #                           [ final predictions ]                           |
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# QUESTION:[ Why Stacking and not just Averging? ]-----------------------------
# -> averaging assumes:                                                       |
#     [ Final predictions = mean(pred_1, pred2, ..., pred_n) ]                |
#     - all the 'predictions' is given the 'same weight'.                     | 
# -> Stacking gives:                                                          |
#    - 'different weights' to the model 'predictions' by modeling each model  |
#       'predictions' and the actual 'predictions'. by another 'model manager'|
#       called -> 'meta-model'.                                               | 
#    - The 'Meta-Model' learns things like this:                              |
#       """                                                                   |    
#         if MLP is usually better on weekends:                               |
#           trust MLP more                                                    |
#         if XGBoost is better during seasonal peaks:                         |
#           trust XGBoost more                                                |
#       """                                                                   |
#     > Example:                                                              |
#       - for linear meta-model, it may learn:                                |
#         """ final = 0.3 * xgb_pred + 0.7 * mlp_pred """                     |
#       - or even more complex relationships if the 'meta-model' is nonlinear |
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
